course: dictionary
lesson: 6168
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word minim has three meanings: a note in music, a tiny drop of liquid, and a stroke of the pen.
explain: «Counting puzzles are about beats: in 4/4 time a bar holds four crotchet beats, a minim lasts two beats and a quaver half a beat, so a minim and two crotchets fill a bar exactly, and a rest still counts as part of the bar.» The clues are beats, bar and crotchet, so minim here is a music note that lasts two beats.
explain: Look for the clue words around the word. Music words like beats, bar and crotchet point to the music meaning. Words like liquid or medicine point to the drop. Words like pen, letters and stroke point to handwriting. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A minim is a music note that lasts two beats in common time (UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland).
fact: In the US, a minim is called a «half note».
fact: In music, a semibreve lasts 4 beats, a minim 2 beats, a crotchet 1 beat and a quaver half a beat.
fact: Two minims fill a 4/4 bar, and one minim equals two crotchets.
fact: In an old measure, a minim is a tiny unit of liquid, about one drop.
fact: In handwriting, a minim is a short downward stroke of the pen, as in the letters m, n, u and i.
exercise: In «a minim lasts two beats», how many beats does a minim last? | *Two beats | One beat | Half a beat | Four beats
exercise: A nurse measures one minim of medicine, about one drop. What does minim mean here? | A short stroke of the pen | A bar of music | A long musical note | *A tiny drop of liquid
exercise: Mia says the letters m, n, u and i each have a minim in them. What is a minim in handwriting? | A long line across the page | A hollow oval with a stem | A drop of ink | *A short downward stroke of the pen
test: Which meaning of minim fits «two minims fill a 4/4 bar»? | *A music note | A tiny drop | A pen stroke
test: A dotted minim lasts how many beats? | *Three | Two | Four | One
exam: Which meaning of minim fits «The doctor measured one minim of medicine»? | *A tiny drop of liquid | A short downward pen stroke | A rest in a song | A note that lasts two beats
